    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1063">

                <pb facs="1109" n="1097" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1097"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.01/5–1245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Lebanese
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Malik</hi>)<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d1063-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-24">May 24, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of May 12, 1945, in which you bring to my attention certain
                    information which you have received from your Government in regard to the
                    proposed landing of French relief forces at Beirut.</p>
                <p>This Government is aware of the circumstances referred to in your note and is
                    giving the matter its careful attention, and earnestly hopes <pb facs="1110"
                        n="1098" xml:id="pg1098"/> that a solution may be reached which will be
                    satisfactory to the Government of the Lebanese Republic.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1063-f1" n="40" type="source" xml:id="d1063-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the Director of the Office of Near Eastern and African Affairs on May 24
                    to the Deputy Director of that Office for delivery to Dr. Malik at San
                    Francisco.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
